‎## Observation
‎Across AI, semiconductors, payments, automation, infrastructure, logistics, online income...
‎
‎**The constant was never the technology.**
‎**The constant was the human making decisions within the technology.**
‎
‎## The Pattern
‎Technology changes.
‎Markets fluctuate.
‎Platforms rise and fall.
‎Infrastructure evolves.
‎
‎**Yet people continue to:**
‎- Interpret information
‎- Make decisions under uncertainty
‎- Build trust
‎- Respond to incentives
‎- Adapt to changing environments
‎- Learn from experience
‎
‎**Technology changes the environment.**
‎**The human factor determines the outcome.**
‎
‎## Intelligence
‎**Purpose of HakunaShortcut:** Not to study technology in isolation.
‎**Purpose:** Understand how humans navigate changing systems.
‎
‎**The Triangle:**
‎**Technology** → Provides capability
‎**Infrastructure** → Provides constraints  
‎**Human Judgment** → Determines direction
‎
‎## Operational Implication
‎**Filter for every future observation:**
‎
‎"What does this reveal about human decision-making within evolving systems?"
‎
‎**If it cannot answer that, it is information. Not yet intelligence.**
‎
